{"acceptance_length": 6.035087719298246, "acceptance_lengths": [5, 5, 11, 2, 1, 1, 2, 1, 11, 4, 4, 3, 2, 7, 1, 13, 3, 13, 1, 3, 6, 4, 4, 4, 6, 1, 9, 9, 4, 1, 3, 3, 16, 1, 1, 16, 4, 6, 3, 9, 8, 8, 15, 13, 2, 4, 4, 4, 4, 10, 16, 15, 3, 16, 1, 9, 9], "accepted_draft_lengths": [4, 4, 10, 1, 0, 0, 1, 0, 10, 3, 3, 2, 1, 6, 0, 12, 2, 12, 0, 2, 5, 3, 3, 3, 5, 0, 8, 8, 3, 0, 2, 2, 15, 0, 0, 15, 3, 5, 2, 8, 7, 7, 14, 12, 1, 3, 3, 3, 3, 9, 15, 14, 2, 15, 0, 8, 8], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 23388434432, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 23388417024, "benchmark": "gsm8k", "completion": "Let's break down the problem step by step to find the total cost of the trip.\n\n---\n\n### **1. Plane Tickets**\n\n- Each ticket costs **$5000**.\n- There are **2 people** (Tom and his wife), so:\n\n$$\n\\text{Total plane cost} = 2 \\times 5000 = \\$10,\\!000\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **2. Hotel Costs**\n\n- **Normal price per day** = $1500\n- The hotel is **20% more expensive** during the busy weekend.\n- So, the **hotel price per day** is:\n\n$$\n1500 + (20\\% \\text{ of } 1500) = 1500 + (0.20 \\times 1500) = 1500 + 300 = \\$1800 \\text{ per day}\n$$\n\n- They are staying for **3 days**, so:\n\n$$\n\\text{Hotel cost} = 3 \\times 1800 = \\$5,\\!400\n$$\n\n---\n\n### **3. Total Cost of the Trip**\n\nNow, add the cost of the plane tickets and the hotel:\n\n$$\n\\text{Total cost} = \\text{Plane cost} + \\text{Hotel cost} = 10,\\!000 + 5,\\!400 = \\boxed{\\$15,\\!400}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{\\$15,\\!400}\n$$", "decode_seconds": 2.0849914541468024, "draft_calls": 57, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 97, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "a53b21494b39f7139d3a04b206a5698dbf22fbd0fa7192f8f9cc577bcf4a59e9", "method": "relay_two", "output_hash": "2f6b5dce7517f0c09550dd60b93ef14536110a60eed7eb55b647e54dbfefe9d8", "output_tokens": 343, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 23521792512, "peak_reserved_memory_bytes": 23787995136, "problem_id": "gsm8k/051ae2b51a5de494", "profile_region